DESCRIPTION:Cliché Day falls on November 3 and has no documented founder\,
  which is itself a cliché of the national-day calendar. The word it point
 s at is more interesting than the observance: it began as a piece of print
 ing hardware\, and it has never entirely stopped meaning one — a cliché
  is a phrase cast once and stamped out ever after.\n\nhttps://todaycelebra
 tes.com/holiday/clich-day/
